==English==

===Etymology===
(1510) Maybe from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|gensor|lang=fro}}, [[comparative]] of {{term|gent||lang=fro|nice, kind, pretty}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|gentius||lang=la|well-born}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈdʒɪn.dʒər.li/|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# [[gently|Gently]]; in a [[delicate]] or [[cautious]] manner.
#: ''He placed the glass jar '''gingerly''' on the concrete step.''
#* {{quote-news
|year=2012
|date=June 3
|author=Nathan Rabin
|title=TV: Review: THE SIMPSONS (CLASSIC): “Mr. Plow” (season 4, episode 9; originally aired 11/19/1992)
|url=http://www.avclub.com/articles/mr-plow,75560/
|page=
|passage=Purchasing a snowplow transforms Homer into a new man. Mr. Burns' laziest employee suddenly becomes an ambitious self-starter who buys ad time on local television at 3:17 A.M (prime viewing hours, Homer '''gingerly''' volunteers, for everyone from alcoholics to the unemployable to garden-variety angry loners) and makes a homemade commercial costarring his family.}}

