===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# very careful or cautious.
#* '''1867''', {{w|Rebecca Harding Davis}}, ''Waiting For The Verdict'', chapter&nbsp;19 “The Valley of the Shadow”, published 1868 in ''The Galaxy'' magazine, volume&nbsp;4, [http://books.google.co.uk/books?id=_iugAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA223 page&nbsp;223]:
#*: But, ther’s somethin’ in the very look and voice of Jeems Strebling, even in his '''gingerly''' walk, that riles all the black drop in me.
#* '''1886''', {{w|Thomas Hardy}}, ''{{w|The Mayor of Casterbridge}}'', [[s:The Mayor of Casterbridge/Chapter 45|chapter&nbsp;45]]:
#*: …penetrating cautiously into dark cellars, sallying forth with '''gingerly''' tread to the garden, now leaf-strewn by autumn winds…
